04:01.560 --> 04:03.520
ConsRouter equals useRouter.

04:03.520 --> 04:05.640
So, we're very explicit in what we're calling.

04:05.640 --> 04:11.280
Then here, we can go router.push once slash Pokedex.

04:11.280 --> 04:13.480
So, we refresh this now,

04:13.480 --> 04:15.480
and we go ahead and go global,

04:15.480 --> 04:19.880
global, swapped to Pokedex. That's it.

04:20.240 --> 04:22.040
That's programmatic navigation.

04:22.040 --> 04:24.240
Main thing being that, what do you do?

04:24.240 --> 04:26.320
You make sure you get the router from

04:26.320 --> 04:27.560
View Router that you can basically,

04:27.560 --> 04:28.920
just like we did from the Composable.

04:28.920 --> 04:30.480
It's a little helper method that says,

04:30.480 --> 04:32.920
hey, we're going to help you do some stuff with the route.

04:32.920 --> 04:35.600
You instantiate it here on line 10.

04:35.600 --> 04:37.960
Then, inside of either our watch or

04:37.960 --> 04:38.960
whatever you need to use it,

04:38.960 --> 04:41.240
it really is just router.push.

04:41.240 --> 04:44.800
The push semantics come from as well,

04:44.800 --> 04:46.520
